##### lab-j  192.168.1.20  scope lab  juniper (TACACS+) #####
# Based on the pull of <time> by alice over netconf (less than a minute ago; the login could
# see secrets) and the standard of <time> (tacctl 0.2.0-test).
#
# What is irregular on lab-j (1 item; the paste fixes 1, leaves 0):
#  1. aaa      ACCESS     missing: the login order tries tacplus (set system authentication-order
#                         tacplus). Fixed by region line 3.
# Consistent: roles. Not planned: netconf, breakglass (walkthrough Steps 6 and 7).
# The standard has nothing for: snmp, mgmt-acl.
# Secrets: 1 present on the device, not changed (--secrets pushes them).
# The pull has no plain view of the configuration: statements that come from a group could not be told
# apart and were not checked (pull the device again to read it).
# The switch undoes this by itself in 5 minutes unless you type the one word after the check (see
# below).
# Paste over ssh, not the console; on a console paste at most twenty lines at a time and watch the
# echo for 'error:'. Pasting the region twice is harmless.
#
# Type this first, on lab-j, and check the name:   show version | match Hostname
# The prompt must end in > (operational mode) before you paste: a prompt ending in # means a
# configuration session is open: stop.
#
##### PASTE FROM HERE: lab-j #####
configure private
# aaa: the authentication order tacctl renders
set system authentication-order tacplus
show | compare | no-more
commit check
commit confirmed 5 comment "tacctl plan lab-j <time> by alice"
##### PASTE TO HERE: lab-j #####
#
# If the first line printed "Users currently editing the configuration" or "error: shared
# configuration database modified": nothing happened; ask that person to commit or roll back, then
# paste again. If any line printed "error:": do not type commit; the switch undoes this by itself
# in 5 minutes.
#
# Check now. In 5 minutes the switch undoes this by itself unless you type one word.
#   From the tacctl server:   tacctl device config pull lab-j --diff     (aaa: ok)
#   In a second terminal:     ssh lab-j, then: show cli authorization | no-more
#                             show configuration system authentication-order | no-more
# When both checks are fine, type this one word yourself:  commit     (before the 5 minutes end)
#
# If your session drops before that, the switch still rolls back when the time runs out (a dropped
# CLI session does not roll back at once): log in again and paste again.
# To undo it after the commit: tacctl device config plan lab-j --backout (its own region to paste;
# tacctl keeps this plan's back-out: after the check pull has replaced the picture, the command
# still prints this plan's, and says which pull it undoes, until the next plan with changes).
# Without tacctl: show system commit, then rollback <n> of the entry just before the one commented
# "tacctl plan lab-j" (the newest entry is that commit itself), then commit.
# Do not: type commit before the check; paste anything outside the banners; paste this into
# another device; use configure exclusive; keep this output in a file after the paste when it
# holds a secret.
